            <div xml:id="d1231">

                <pb facs="0998" n="882" xml:id="pg882"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 812.00/2930.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Consul at Ciudad
                            Juárez to the Secretary of
                    State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Ciudad Juárez</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">via
                                El Paso, Tex.</hi>)</placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1912-02-27">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 27, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Ciudad Juárez peacefully surrendered to-day to General Campa with 800 men. Good
                    order prevails.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Edwards.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
